00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.632
with people close to the best practices,

39
00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:41.668
I think there could be a big uplift

40
00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:45.305
still for mastering these best practices

41
00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:47.740
and knowing how they drive that amazing productivity

42
00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:50.477
that I'm seeing many developers have using Claude Code.

43
00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:53.179
So as we start to talk about those best practices,

44
00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:57.383
a key tip for working with Claude Code
is providing clear context

45
00:01:57.383 --> 00:02:00.320
to help Claude code achieve the task you want efficiently.

46
00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:03.189
This means pointing Claude code to the relevant files,

47
00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:06.993
clearly describing the features
and functionality that you want

48
00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:09.362
and making sure that you're properly extending

49
00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:11.564
the capabilities of Claude code

50
00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:14.200
with MCP servers and other tools in that ecosystem.

51
00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:18.104
In this course, you'll apply those
best practices to three different examples.

52
00:02:18.104 --> 00:02:19.973
We'll start with a RAG chatbot

53
00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:21.341
and you'll implement the features from

54
00:02:21.341 --> 00:02:22.942
the front end to the back end,

55
00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:26.212
including refactoring code, writing tests,

56
00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:28.114
and then using the GitHub integration to

57
00:02:28.114 --> 00:02:30.049
